From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: TheKit <thekit@disroot.org>
Date: Mon, 20 Jul 2026 12:15:49 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] surfaceflinger: Always request client composition

hwcomposer is reached through HWC2On1Adapter, which expects a framebuffer
target buffer on every frame. When no layer required client composition
surfaceflinger skipped rendering and queued nothing, leaving the adapter
without a target.
---
 services/surfaceflinger/CompositionEngine/src/Display.cpp | 5 ++++-
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/services/surfaceflinger/CompositionEngine/src/Display.cpp b/services/surfaceflinger/CompositionEngine/src/Display.cpp
index 5144c967ed..39421d776b 100644
--- a/services/surfaceflinger/CompositionEngine/src/Display.cpp
+++ b/services/surfaceflinger/CompositionEngine/src/Display.cpp
@@ -303,7 +303,10 @@ void Display::applyCompositionStrategy(const std::optional<DeviceRequestedChange
 
     // Determine what type of composition we are doing from the final state
     auto& state = editState();
-    state.usesClientComposition = anyLayersRequireClientComposition();
+    // Waydroid: hwcomposer runs through HWC2On1Adapter, which always expects a
+    // framebuffer target, so keep client composition on even when no layer asks
+    // for it. Device composition is still selected per layer.
+    state.usesClientComposition = true;
     state.usesDeviceComposition = !allLayersRequireClientComposition();
 }
 
